    {
      "id": "ab-tl-a",
      "type": "sharedSection",
      "props": {
        "sectionId": "timeline",
        "values": {
          "entries": [
            {
              "title": "Established",
              "years": "1906–1940",
              "text": "<strong>1906</strong>: Louis Ballard, a skilled blacksmith and carriage maker, offers automotive repair services.\n\n<strong>1918</strong>: With a rising demand for repair services, Louis founded L.H. Ballard’s Garage on Howe Avenue in Millbury, Massachusetts, with his son, Harold, joining as his assistant. It was the first auto repair shop between Worcester and Blackstone.\n\n<strong>1928</strong>: Expanding his business, Louis opened Ballard Motor Sales, a Chrysler dealership, on a neighboring property.\n\n<strong>1940</strong>: By this time, Louis employed seven full-time mechanics, with Harold playing an integral role in the business."
            },
            {
              "title": "Family-Owned",
              "years": "1948–1982",
              "text": "<strong>1948</strong>: Harold Ballard and his wife, Minnie, took ownership of the dealership, earning the Chrysler Medal of Merit Award in 1951.\n\n<strong>1960</strong>: Robert “Bob” Picking joined the dealership after serving four years in the U.S. Navy.\n\n<strong>1982</strong>: Harold and Minnie’s niece, Janet Grahn, and her nephew, John Picking, began working at the dealership."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "children": []
    },
